    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d486">

                <pb facs="0613" n="505" xml:id="pg505"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McDonald to Mr. Gresham.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Teheran, Persia</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-10-29"><hi rendition="#italic">October 29, 1893</hi></date>.
                        (Received December 6.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 30.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Touching my correspondence with His Majesty
                    concerning the Oroomiah murder, I have the honor to forward, in addition to what
                    has already been sent, as inclosures, a copy of my last note to the prime
                    minister, and also of one from the foreign minister to me.</p>
                <p>I beg to state that the missionaries are desirous that the Shah’s assuring letter
                    be published for the benefit of their friends at home; and if there is no reason
                    to the contrary, I would second their request that it be given to the press.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alex. McDonald.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d486-a1.xml" xpointer="d486-a1"/>
